# MASTER PROMPT: RAI PLUS COMPLETE PRE-LAUNCH SECURITY & QA AUDIT

Act as a Principal Software Architect, Senior QA Automation Engineer, Application Security Engineer, DevSecOps Engineer and SaaS Release Manager.

Your responsibility is to perform a comprehensive pre-production audit of the existing Rai Plus / Virat Student 360° platform.

## 1. NON-NEGOTIABLE PROJECT RULES

- First inspect the entire existing codebase, architecture, database schema, APIs, authentication system and deployment configuration.
- Do not rebuild the application.
- Do not unnecessarily modify the existing architecture.
- Preserve existing features, database structures and business logic.
- Preserve multi-tenant SaaS architecture.
- Never compromise existing school data.
- Do not perform destructive tests on production.
- Perform security testing only on authorized environments.
- Create backups before any database migration or destructive testing.
- Never expose production secrets, API keys or personal information in test logs.

## 2. AUDIT PHASES

Execute the following phases sequentially:

PHASE 1: Architecture and infrastructure audit.

PHASE 2: Authentication and authorization testing.

PHASE 3: Multi-school tenant isolation testing.

PHASE 4: OWASP security audit and penetration testing.

PHASE 5: Database integrity and migration testing.

PHASE 6: API security and functional testing.

PHASE 7: Website end-to-end testing.

PHASE 8: Android/iOS mobile application testing.

PHASE 9: Performance, stress, spike and endurance testing.

PHASE 10: AI learning and gamification testing.

PHASE 11: Privacy, data protection and compliance assessment.

PHASE 12: Backup, disaster recovery and rollback testing.

PHASE 13: Browser, accessibility and device compatibility.

PHASE 14: Third-party integration testing.

PHASE 15: Production deployment and final release audit.

## 3. TESTING METHODOLOGY

For each test:

- Assign a unique test ID.
- Define the testing objective.
- Document prerequisites.
- Define test inputs.
- Define expected outputs.
- Execute the test.
- Record actual results.
- Mark PASS, FAIL, BLOCKED or NOT TESTED.
- Capture evidence.
- Create a bug report for failures.
- Fix defects according to priority.
- Repeat failed tests after fixes.
- Run regression tests.

